---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
---

<Layout
  path="/network"
  title="Arbitrum Network Subgraph endpoint - Nuthatch"
  description="A public, rate-limited GraphQL endpoint for indexers managing Arbitrum One allocations on The Graph Network."
>
  <section class="page network-page">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="section-label">The Graph Network · Arbitrum One</p>
      <h1>A public Network Subgraph endpoint.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Indexers need a current Network Subgraph to allocate, unallocate, close, and reconcile
        allocations. The Night's Watch now keeps one available for that job.
      </p>

      <div class="endpoint-card">
        <p class="endpoint-label">GraphQL endpoint</p>
        <CopyBlock command="https://network.thenightswatch.dev/graphql" size="lg" />
        <p class="endpoint-note">POST GraphQL requests directly to this URL. No API key is required.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card-label">For indexer-agent</p>
          <p>Set <code>INDEXER_AGENT_NETWORK_SUBGRAPH_ENDPOINT</code> to the endpoint above and leave the local deployment unset.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card-label">For indexer-service-rs</p>
          <p>Set <code>[subgraphs.network].query_url</code> to the endpoint. Do not set a local <code>deployment_id</code> at the same time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card-label">Freshness</p>
          <p>The endpoint publishes the upstream <code>_meta</code> block and is kept close to the Arbitrum head. It is rate-limited, not authenticated.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What it serves</h2>
      <p>
        The live route serves the fixed GraphQL documents used by the indexer agent, indexer-service-rs,
        and TAP monitor: allocations, indexers, deployments, graph-network parameters, epochs,
        <code>paymentsEscrowAccounts</code>, and <code>paymentsEscrowTransactions</code>.
        BigInt, Bytes, IDs, pagination, block pins, and <code>_meta</code> follow graph-node wire semantics.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p class="card-label">A note on the first deployment</p>
        <p>
          The public route currently fronts a fresh, verified grafted Network Subgraph deployment while
          the permanent Nuthatch-native facade completes its full-history archive backfill. The public
          contract is the same GraphQL contract indexers need today; the native implementation will
          replace the upstream route after parity and freshness checks pass.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="signoff">
        If your indexer is stuck waiting for a local sync, use the endpoint above and keep an eye on
        <code>_meta.block.number</code>. Questions and operational reports belong in
        <a href="https://github.com/nightswatchhq/nuthatch/issues" rel="noopener">Nuthatch issues</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .network-page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem); }
  .network-page h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .lead { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 38rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .endpoint-card { background: var(--bg-elev); border: 1px solid var(--border-hi); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .endpoint-label, .card-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 0.65rem; }
  .endpoint-note { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.88rem; margin: 0.8rem 0 0; }
  .network-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .card { padding: 1.15rem; }
  .card p:last-child, .callout p:last-child { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
  .network-page h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .network-page h2 + p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .callout { border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); background: var(--bg-inset); padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .signoff { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 42rem) { .network-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
